"""Approximate a detector of explicit encoding and formatting notation.

NULs, UTF-8 byte escapes, numeric HTML entities, escaped apostrophes and
mojibake-like Latin-1 characters are positive. Doubled backslashes are
positive in escaped text but negative near TeX mathematics; TeX layout
commands are also negative. Most ordinary text receives zero. The small
remaining rules cover diff markers and document headers/import directives.
