"""Approximate extra indentation in line-rendered code, plus a zero response.

Tabs after line numbers, escaped-newline indentation, whitespace-type changes,
and comment/diff margins are positive. Ordinary line-start spaces are not.
Nonbreaking-space indentation is positive in backtick-marked text. A separate
negative rule covers repeated/padded zeros, endings in 30, and some zeros next
to letters or decimal points. Only the latest 160 characters of a line are
remembered; document boundaries reset that state.
