Count n's in the spelling, using transliteration (Mandarin pinyin for Han).
Short n-rich fragments receive the largest response. Common words and the
clusters 'ing' and 'ion' have weaker responses than literal spelling predicts.
There are also separate responses to digit nine and four-space indentation.
Incomplete Unicode fragments get a small fallback; context is not modeled.
These are approximate spelling rules, not a word-by-word activation table.
