"""Approximate a numeric-table and column-boundary response.

Decimal/grouped numbers, nearby digits, and horizontal padding strengthen
estimates on whitespace, pipes, alignment ampersands, and field punctuation.
Repeated columns and LaTeX uncertainty/ellipsis notation get extra weight.
The first digit after whitespace inherits half its boundary estimate;
a digit immediately after a parenthesized percentage is another field start.
Other tokens return zero. Keep only recent text, resetting at each document.
